  "output": "Now I have a complete picture. Here's the full performance analysis:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis\n\nThis is a Rails/Hotwire app — the \"unnecessary React re-renders\" category doesn't apply.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Missing Database Indexes (Highest Impact)\n\nThe admin dashboard fires **15+ COUNT queries** on every load against unindexed columns. These do full table scans.\n\n**Missing indexes on `conversions`:**\n```ruby\n# No index on created_at or status — every dashboard query scans the full table\nConversion.where(created_at: now.beginning_of_day..)   # full scan\nConversion.where(status: :completed)                    # full scan\n```\n\n**Missing indexes on `users`:**\n```ruby\nUser.where(plan: :pro)           # full scan — no index on plan\nUser.where(created_at: 7.days.ago..)  # full scan — no index on created_at\nUser.where(confirmed_at: nil)    # full scan — no index on confirmed_at\n```\n\n**Fix — add a migration:**\n```ruby\nadd_index :conversions, :created_at\nadd_index :conversions, :status\nadd_index :users, :plan\nadd_index :users, :created_at\nadd_index :users, :confirmed_at\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Admin Dashboard — 15 Uncached COUNT Queries (`admin/dashboard_controller.rb:7–49`)\n\nEvery admin page load hits the DB 15 times. These numbers don't need sub-second accuracy.\n\n```ruby\n# Current: 15 separate queries, no cache\n@total_users      = User.count\n@users_today      = User.where(created_at: now.beginning_of_day..).count\n# ... 13 more\n\n# Fix: cache the whole block for 5 minutes\ndef index\n  now = Time.current\n  stats = Rails.cache.fetch('admin_dashboard_stats', expires_in: 5.minutes) do\n    {\n      total_users:           User.count,\n      users_today:           User.where(created_at: now.beginning_of_day..).count,\n      users_this_week:       User.where(created_at: 7.days.ago..).count,\n      users_this_month:      User.where(created_at: 30.days.ago..).count,\n      confirmed_users:       User.where.not(confirmed_at: nil).count,\n      unconfirmed_users:     User.where(confirmed_at: nil).count,\n      google_users:          User.where(provider: \"google_oauth2\").count,\n      email_users:           User.where(provider: nil).count,\n      pro_users:             User.where(plan: :pro).count,\n      free_users:            User.where(plan: :free).count,\n      total_conversions:     Conversion.count,\n      conversions_today:     Conversion.where(created_at: now.beginning_of_day..).count,\n      conversions_this_week: Conversion.where(created_at: 7.days.ago..).count,\n      completed_conversions: Conversion.where(status: :completed).count,\n      failed_conversions:    Conversion.where(status: :failed).count,\n    }\n  end\n  stats.each { |k, v| instance_variable_set(\"@#{k}\", v) }\n\n  # Chart data and recent activity still run live (they're fast/bounded)\n  @top_tools          = Conversion.where(created_at: 30.days.ago..).group(:tool_name).order(\"count_all DESC\").limit(10).count\n  @conversions_by_day = Conversion.where(created_at: 30.days.ago..).group(\"DATE(created_at)\").order(\"DATE(created_at)\").count\n  @users_by_day       = User.where(created_at: 30.days.ago..).group(\"DATE(created_at)\").order(\"DATE(created_at)\").count\n  @recent_users       = User.order(created_at: :desc).limit(10)\n  @recent_conversions = Conversion.includes(:user).order(created_at: :desc).limit(10)\nend\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Unbounded Query in Conversions Index (`conversions_controller.rb:5`)\n\n```ruby\n# Current: loads ALL of a user's conversions — no limit\n@conversions = current_user.conversions.order(created_at: :desc)\n\n# Fix: paginate (kaminari is already in the admin controller)\n@conversions = current_user.conversions.order(created_at: :desc).page(params[:page]).per(20)\n```\n\nA user with 500+ conversions currently loads them all into memory and renders every row. The view already handles an empty state so it just needs the paginator added.\n\n---\n\n### 4. O(n) Linear Scan Per Row in Conversions View (`conversions/index.html.erb:36`)\n\n```erb\n<%# Current: ToolRegistry.tools.find runs a 28-item array scan for every row %>\n<% tool_meta = ToolRegistry.tools.find { |t| t[:class_name] == conversion.tool_name } %>\n```\n\n**Fix — add a lookup method to `ToolRegistry`:**\n```ruby\n# tool_registry.rb\ndef self.by_class_name\n  @by_class_name ||= tools.index_by { |t| t[:class_name] }\nend\n```\n\nThen in both the view and `conversions_controller.rb#show`:\n```erb\n<%# conversions/index.html.erb — build once, look up per row %>\n<% tool_lookup = ToolRegistry.by_class_name %>\n<% @conversions.each do |conversion| %>\n  <% tool_meta = tool_lookup[conversion.tool_name] %>\n```\n\n```ruby\n# conversions_controller.rb:39\n@tool_meta = ToolRegistry.by_class_name[@conversion.tool_name]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. Analytics Controller — 3 Queries Where 1 Suffices (`analytics_controller.rb:6–11`)\n\n```ruby\n# Current: 3 round-trips\n@total_conversions = current_user.conversions.count\n@recent_conversions = current_user.conversions.where('created_at > ?', 30.days.ago).count\n@older_conversions  = current_user.conversions.where('created_at BETWEEN ? AND ?', 60.days.ago, 30.days.ago).count\n\n# Fix: one query with PostgreSQL conditional aggregates\ntotal, recent, older = current_user.conversions.pick(\n  Arel.sql(<<~SQL)\n    COUNT(*),\n    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE created_at > NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days'),\n    COUNT(*) FILTER (WHERE created_at BETWEEN NOW() - INTERVAL '60 days' AND NOW() - INTERVAL '30 days')\n  SQL\n)\n@total_conversions  = total\n@recent_conversions = recent\n@older_conversions  = older\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. Cloudinary Double API Call in Download (`conversions_controller.rb:163–182`)\n\n```ruby\n# Current: tries \"raw\" type first, on 404 retries with \"image\" type — 2 API calls for old uploads\n[\"raw\", \"image\"].each do |resource_type|\n  Cloudinary::Api.resource(key, resource_type: resource_type)  # API call\n  # ...\nend\n```\n\nIf you store the `resource_type` in the `Conversion#options` jsonb column at upload time, you can skip the probe:\n\n```ruby\n# At upload time in tool (base_tool.rb or wherever blobs are stored):\nconversion.update(options: conversion.options.merge(cloudinary_resource_type: \"raw\"))\n\n# In download:\nresource_type = @conversion.options&.dig(\"cloudinary_resource_type\") || \"raw\"\n# No API.resource probe needed — go straight to cloudinary_url\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. Cleanup Job — Slow Destroy Loop (`cleanup_conversions_job.rb:26–31`)\n\n```ruby\n# Current: one destroy per record — fine for callbacks, but count query is redundant\ndef purge_conversions(conversions)\n  count = conversions.count   # ← extra COUNT query\n  conversions.find_each { |c| c.destroy }\n  count\nend\n\n# Fix: count while iterating\ndef purge_conversions(conversions)\n  count = 0\n  conversions.find_each { |c| c.destroy; count += 1 }\n  count\nend\n```\n\nThe individual `destroy` calls are unavoidable if you need Active Storage to purge blobs. No change needed there.\n\n---\n\n### Summary by Impact\n\n| Issue | Impact | Effort |\n|---|---|---|\n| Missing DB indexes on `created_at`/`status`/`plan` | High — full table scans | Low — one migration |\n| Admin dashboard uncached stats (15 queries) | High — every admin page load | Low — wrap in `Rails.cache.fetch` |\n| Unbounded conversions index query | Medium — memory + slow render at scale | Low — add `.page().per()` |\n| `ToolRegistry.by_class_name` lookup | Low — in-memory, 28 items | Low — add one method |\n| Analytics 3→1 query | Low — user-scoped, fast | Medium — SQL change |\n| Cloudinary double probe | Low — affects download path | Medium — requires schema change |\n\nThe indexes + dashboard cache give you the most value for the least code.\n",
